This file imports the fixed-point theorem and records Eilenberg's criterion. An approximable endomap has a unique fixed point when a sequence of approximable maps is constantly bottom at stage zero, is increasing, has each element as the least upper bound of the values of the sequence at that element, and satisfies the commutation that the next approximant after the map equals the next approximant after the map after the current approximant. The comment explains existence by the least fixed point and uniqueness by an induction along the approximants, using the commutation twice and the least-upper-bound property of the scheme.
